msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"JAGS -- Just Another Gibbs Sampler -- is software for general purpose "
"Bayesian inference. One can specify a model using JAGS syntax and let JAGS "
"draw samples from the posterior distribution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "References"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "R Packages"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Enter the desired model. Columns in the data can be directly referred to. If "
"these contain spaces, then the reference must also contain spaces."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "A box that automatically detects which parameters the model contains."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The parameters for which the MCMC samples are stored. Only available when "
"'Show results for' is set to 'selected parameters'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Determines which parameters are shown in tables and plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Sometimes it is practical to directly specify the observed data without "
"loading a data set. Here such observations can be listed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Each row has a 'Parameter', the name to be used in the JAGS model code, and "
"an 'R Code', the value for the data. This value can also be R code."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Determines the color scheme of the plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"If checked, the samples of different chains are aggregated in density plots "
"and histograms. If unchecked, there are separate colors per chain."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Show a legend in the plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show the marginal density of the posterior samples for each parameter "
"selected under 'Show results for these parameters'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show the marginal histogram of the posterior samples for each parameter "
"selected under 'Show results for these parameters'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show a trace plot of the posterior samples for each parameter selected under "
"'Show results for these parameters'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Plot the autocorrelation of the posterior samples for each parameter "
"selected under 'Show results for these parameters'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The maximum number of lags to show in the autocorrelation plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Whether to display the autocorrelation as a bar at each lag, or as a line "
"that connects subsequent lags."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show a matrix plot of all pairs of parameters. Only shows output when more "
"than 1 parameter is sampled."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show a density plot or a histogram on the diagonal entries of the scatter "
"plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Show a hexagonal bivariate density plot, or a contour plot on the off-"
"diagonal entries of the scatter plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Each tab specifies a set of custom results (a plot and a table) for one "
"parameter. Up to 10 tabs can be added."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "For which parameter to show custom results."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Select a parameter from the model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Optionally specify a subset of the parameter, e.g., 1:4 or 1, 3, 5:8."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Optionally, superimpose data on the plots. Only available when a data set is "
"loaded."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "A scale variable in the data set to superimpose on the plots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "A nominal variable in the data set used to split the superimposed data."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The type of plot to show. Currently, only 'None' or 'Stacked density' are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The metric used to order the parameters in the stacked density plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Whether to shade an interval in the plot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The interval to shade: a credible interval, a highest density interval "
"(HDI), or a custom interval."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Shade the area between the lower and the upper bound."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The type of plot to show for the superimposed data. Only available when data "
"are superimposed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The method used to determine the bin width of the histogram."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The number of bins, when the bin width type is 'Manual'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Specify which statistics are computed for each parameter and shown in a "
"table."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The average value of the posterior samples."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The middle value of the posterior samples."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The value of the posterior distribution with the highest density."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The standard deviation of the posterior samples."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The potential scale reduction factor, used to diagnose convergence of the "
"MCMC chains."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"An estimate of the number of independent samples from the posterior "
"distribution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"An interval within which a certain percentage of the posterior samples fall."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Highest Density Interval: the narrowest interval containing a specified "
"percentage of the posterior samples."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The proportion of the posterior samples that fall within a user-defined "
"interval."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"For each parameter in the model, it is possible to specify an initial value. "
"Initial values can be numbers, but also R code. The R code is evaluated "
"separately for each chain, so `rnorm(1)` yields different initial values for "
"each chain."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Each row has a 'Parameter' of the model and an 'R Code', its initial value."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Unlike some other software programs, JASP first draws 'No. burnin samples' "
"from the posterior distribution and afterward 'No. samples', keeping every "
"nth sample as specified by 'Thinning'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The number of samples to draw from the posterior distribution that are used "
"for results (tables, plots)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The number of samples to draw from the posterior distribution and "
"immediately discard."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Every nth value of 'No. samples' is kept for the results, where n is given "
"by 'Thinning'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "The number of MCMC chains to run."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"By default, 'all monitored parameters' is selected which implies that JASP "
"stores the MCMC samples for all parameters in the model. However, for large "
"JAGS models storing all MCMC samples may take too much memory. By selecting "
"'selected parameters', one can first decide for which parameters the MCMC "
"samples should be stored, and in a next box, decide which of these "
"parameters should be shown in the results."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"Set a seed for JAGS. The same seed and model specification yields the same "
"results."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Show the Deviance statistic."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"The CSV file to save the MCMC samples to. The samples are only written when "
"'Sync Samples' is on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid "Sync Samples"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "JAGS|"
msgid ""
"When on, the MCMC samples are written to the export file, and written again "
"each time the analysis is rerun. Toggled with the 'Sync Samples' button."
msgstr ""
